  "worked_solution": "Starting with the initial terms ${a}_{1}=6,$ and ${a}_{2}=3,$ we compute the next terms using the recursive formula until we reach the fourth term.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =6 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =3 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{a}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3+\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 6=\\frac{3}{2}+2=\\frac{7}{2} \\\\ {a}_{4} & =\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{3}+\\frac{1}{3}{a}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}+\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 3=\\frac{7}{4}+1=\\frac{11}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fourth term is ${a}_{4}=\\frac{11}{4}.$",
